# Methodology

## Overall Pipeline

```text
Data Collection
      ↓
Data Cleaning
      ↓
Resampling / Interpolation
      ↓
Feature Engineering
      ↓
Lagging
      ↓
COVID-19 Treatment
      ↓
Chronological Train/Test Split
      ↓
TimeSeriesSplit
      ↓
Hyperparameter Tuning
      ↓
Model Training
      ↓
Out-of-Sample Forecast
      ↓
Performance Evaluation
```

## Chronological Evaluation

Random train-test splitting is avoided because future observations must not enter the training data.

### Macroeconomic Data

```text
Training: 2008–2022
Testing:  2023–2025
```

### Equity Data

```text
Training: January 2022 – December 2025
Testing:  January 2026 – May 2026
```

## COVID-19 Treatment

2020 is treated asymmetrically:

```text
2020 Target
    ↓
Excluded

2020 Lagged Information
    ↓
Retained
```

This allows the model to use historical information from the COVID shock when forecasting the 2021 recovery without allowing the extreme 2020 target observation to directly distort training.

## TimeSeriesSplit

Hyperparameter tuning uses time-series-aware cross-validation rather than random K-fold validation.

```text
Fold 1: Train → Test
Fold 2: Train ──→ Test
Fold 3: Train ─────→ Test
Fold 4: Train ─────────→ Test
```

The fundamental rule is:

**Past → Future**

and never:

**Future → Past**

## Evaluation

The primary macroeconomic metric is **Out-of-Sample R²**.

```text
OOS-R² > 0
→ Better than the naive mean benchmark

OOS-R² < 0
→ Worse than the naive mean benchmark
```

Equity forecasting additionally evaluates prediction error using MSE.
